    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d195-a2">

                <pb facs="0281" n="247" xml:id="pg247"/>

                <head>I. <lb/>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Copy of a resolution of the Senate of the United States,
                        passed February</hi> 8, 1870.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">In the Senate of the United
                                States,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1870-02-08"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >February</hi> 8, 1870.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">Resolved</hi>, That the President be requested, if not
                    incompatible with the public interests, to invite a correspondence with Great
                    Britain and other foreign powers, with a view to promote the adoption, by the
                    legislatures of the several powers, of a common unit and standard of an
                    international gold coinage, and that such correspondence be submitted to
                    Congress for its information and action.</p>
                <p>Attest:</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>GEO. C. GORHAM, <hi rendition="#italic"
                    >Secretary</hi>.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
